WEBVTT

00:10.468 --> 00:11.970
[Mike sighs] That's better.

00:19.644 --> 00:21.229
You don't need it.

00:24.107 --> 00:25.525
Still pretty?

00:25.608 --> 00:27.402
Yeah!

00:27.485 --> 00:29.362
Pretty. Really pretty.

00:35.702 --> 00:36.703
El?

00:37.871 --> 00:38.997
Yes?

00:40.165 --> 00:43.251
[stammers] Um, I'm happy you're home.

00:44.085 --> 00:45.837
Me, too.

00:52.218 --> 00:53.970
- [door opens]
- Guys!

00:54.054 --> 00:55.680
[panting] It's Lucas,
I think he's in trouble.

00:57.682 --> 00:59.559
Do you remember how he said
he was looking for the gate?

00:59.642 --> 01:01.227
- [Mike] Yeah.
- What if he found it?

01:01.311 --> 01:03.313
[Lucas shouting indistinctly on radio]

01:04.314 --> 01:05.356
What's he saying?

01:05.440 --> 01:07.484
I don't know, he's way out of range.

01:08.193 --> 01:09.527
[Lucas] ...son of a bitch!

01:09.611 --> 01:12.739
Lucas, if you can hear us, slow down.
We can't understand you.

01:12.822 --> 01:15.408
Yes, I copy!
Do you?

01:15.492 --> 01:17.243
They know about Eleven!

01:17.327 --> 01:19.370
Get out of there!
They know about Eleven!

01:19.454 --> 01:21.956
The bad men are coming!
All of them!

01:22.040 --> 01:24.709
Do you hear me?
The bad men are coming!

01:24.793 --> 01:26.461
"Mad hen."
Does that mean anything to you?

01:26.544 --> 01:27.879
Like a code name or something?

01:27.962 --> 01:30.423
- [Lucas] The bad men are coming!
- "Bad men."

01:30.507 --> 01:32.133
- Bad men!
- [radio static]

01:32.217 --> 01:34.135
[gasps] Stay here.

01:43.436 --> 01:44.729
[Mike] What's that guy doing?

01:44.813 --> 01:46.731
You don't think...

01:48.566 --> 01:50.985
Well, I know she and Steve
have been spending some time together,

01:51.069 --> 01:52.237
- so I thought maybe--
- Mom!

01:52.320 --> 01:54.114
[stammers] Well, is he home?

01:54.197 --> 01:55.240
- Maybe you could ask him?
- Mom!

01:55.323 --> 01:56.616
I'm sorry,
can you just hold on, please?

01:56.699 --> 01:58.827
Michael, I'm on the phone.
I've told you a million times--

01:58.910 --> 02:00.829
- Did you schedule any repairs?
- What?

02:00.912 --> 02:03.581
Is there anyone supposed to come
and do repairs on the house?

02:14.050 --> 02:15.301
I don't understand.
Is there something wrong--

02:15.385 --> 02:17.637
- No, Mom, nothing's wrong in the house.
- [Dustin] Mike!

02:17.720 --> 02:19.681
- One second.
- [yells] Mike!

02:19.764 --> 02:23.685
We need to leave...
[panting] right now.

02:25.687 --> 02:27.730
- [sighs]
- Michael!

02:28.481 --> 02:31.609
If anyone asks where I am,
I've left the country.

02:31.693 --> 02:32.777
What?

02:36.406 --> 02:37.740
[Dustin grunts]

02:58.261 --> 03:00.513
[Dustin] Go, go, go,
go, go, go, go, go, go!

03:05.143 --> 03:07.186
- [engines starting]
- [tires screeching]

03:11.065 --> 03:12.358
Oh, my God.
Oh, my God.

03:12.442 --> 03:14.819
- Oh, my God. Oh, my God. Oh, my God.
- [Lucas on radio] Dustin!

03:14.903 --> 03:16.779
Dustin, do you copy?

03:16.863 --> 03:18.698
Yeah, Lucas, they're on us.

03:18.781 --> 03:20.408
- Where are you?
- Cornwallis.

03:20.491 --> 03:21.784
Meet me at Elm and Cherry!

03:21.868 --> 03:23.494
Copy. Elm and Cherry!

03:23.578 --> 03:24.787
Okay.

03:32.420 --> 03:34.213
- Shit!
- This way, come on!

03:36.716 --> 03:38.551
- [indistinct singing]
- [bicycle bell ringing]

03:39.469 --> 03:40.595
Out of the way!

03:40.678 --> 03:42.305
- Out of the way!
- [ringing continues]

03:49.854 --> 03:51.022
- [Mike] Lucas!
- Where are they?

03:51.105 --> 03:52.398
- [stammers] I don't know.
- I think we lost them.

03:52.482 --> 03:54.943
- [tires screeching]
- Go, go, go, go, go!

03:55.026 --> 03:56.444
[Dustin yelling]

03:57.445 --> 03:59.113
[Mike] Go, go, go, go, go!

03:59.197 --> 04:01.532
- Faster, faster!
- Shit, shit, shit, shit, shit!

04:05.787 --> 04:06.871
[yelling]

04:16.756 --> 04:18.758
- [van crashing]
- [tires screeching]

04:52.542 --> 04:54.127
Holy... holy shit!

04:54.210 --> 04:56.587
Did... did you see
what she did to that van?

04:56.671 --> 04:57.755
No, Dustin, we missed it.

04:57.839 --> 05:00.341
- [stammering] I mean that was...
- [Lucas] Awesome.

05:00.425 --> 05:02.343
[Lucas panting]

05:02.427 --> 05:04.095
It was awesome.

05:10.977 --> 05:14.814
Everything I said
about you being a traitor and stuff...

05:16.107 --> 05:17.525
I was wrong.

05:20.862 --> 05:22.363
I'm sorry.

05:26.909 --> 05:28.077
Friends...

05:29.329 --> 05:30.872
friends don't lie.

05:33.374 --> 05:35.084
I'm sorry, too.

05:36.586 --> 05:37.628
[Mike] Me, too.

05:50.892 --> 05:52.894
[theme music playing]

07:08.094 --> 07:09.137
Hey.

07:09.220 --> 07:11.681
Jonathan?
Jesus, what... what happened?

07:11.764 --> 07:12.932
- [Callahan] Ma'am...
- I'm fine.

07:13.015 --> 07:14.475
Why is he wearing handcuffs?

07:14.559 --> 07:16.686
Well, your boy assaulted a police officer.
That's why.

07:16.769 --> 07:19.063
- Take them off.
- I am afraid I cannot do that.

07:19.147 --> 07:21.232
- Take them off!
- You heard her. Take 'em off.

07:21.315 --> 07:26.779
Chief, I get everyone's emotional here,
but there's something you need to see.

07:33.703 --> 07:34.787
What is this?

07:34.871 --> 07:36.456
Why don't you ask your son?
We found it in his car.

07:36.539 --> 07:38.166
- What?
- Why are you going through my car?

07:38.249 --> 07:40.042
Is that really the question
you should be asking right now?

07:40.543 --> 07:42.211
I wanna see you in my office.

07:42.295 --> 07:43.629
You won't believe me.

07:45.590 --> 07:47.717
[softly] Why don't you give me a try?

07:49.010 --> 07:51.512
Mike? Mike?

07:55.183 --> 07:56.392
[sighs]

08:11.282 --> 08:12.617
[doorbell rings]

08:12.700 --> 08:14.827
Yeah, just a minute, please!

08:15.745 --> 08:18.581
- [under breath] Jiminy Christmas.
- [doorbell continues ringing]

08:19.499 --> 08:20.958
Hold your horses.

08:24.962 --> 08:26.005
Mr. Wheeler?

08:26.088 --> 08:27.715
Yes?

08:34.472 --> 08:36.849
[men speaking indistinctly]

09:09.173 --> 09:11.551
[Karen stuttering] I don't understand.

09:11.634 --> 09:14.011
You think my son is hiding this girl?

09:14.095 --> 09:15.221
What happened to her hair?

09:15.304 --> 09:17.848
We just need to know
if you've seen her in the past week.

09:17.932 --> 09:21.143
- No, no.
- Absolutely not.

09:21.227 --> 09:22.937
Our son with a girl?

09:23.020 --> 09:25.314
[chuckles] I mean, believe me,

09:25.398 --> 09:28.734
if he had a girl sleeping in this house,
we'd know about it.

09:28.818 --> 09:30.403
Wouldn't we?

09:30.486 --> 09:31.487
[Karen sighs]

09:31.571 --> 09:33.322
This girl...

09:33.406 --> 09:34.448
what has she done?

09:34.532 --> 09:36.284
I'm afraid I can't answer that.

09:36.367 --> 09:37.660
- Oh, my God, is she Russian?
- [stammers]

09:37.743 --> 09:40.871
- You can't treat us like this.
- I need you to stay calm.

09:40.955 --> 09:42.665
You come into my house,

09:42.748 --> 09:45.251
and you tell me that my son
is hiding some girl,

09:45.334 --> 09:48.462
and that he's in danger,
but you can't tell us why?

09:48.546 --> 09:51.382
And you, what,
you expect me to remain, what, calm?

09:59.932 --> 10:01.309
[sighs]

10:02.685 --> 10:05.062
I understand how upsetting this is.

10:06.105 --> 10:08.357
I wish we could tell you more...

10:09.692 --> 10:14.739
but I can tell you that your son,
Michael, is in real danger.

10:17.283 --> 10:18.659
We want to help him.

10:18.743 --> 10:21.537
We will help him.
I give you my word.

10:23.372 --> 10:25.499
But in order for me to do that...

10:27.126 --> 10:28.919
you have to trust me.

10:31.380 --> 10:33.049
Will you trust me?

10:38.721 --> 10:40.014
Good.

10:40.097 --> 10:41.265
Now...

10:43.184 --> 10:45.645
do you have any idea
where your son might have gone?

10:49.857 --> 10:52.985
[Lucas] This is Randolph Road, right here.

10:53.069 --> 10:56.614
The fence starts here,
and goes all the way around.

10:57.531 --> 10:59.659
And this is the lab right here.

10:59.742 --> 11:01.202
The gate's gotta be in there somewhere.

11:01.285 --> 11:02.328
It's gotta be.

11:02.411 --> 11:04.288
[Dustin] Well, who owns Hawkins Lab?

11:04.372 --> 11:05.790
The sign says "Department of Energy."

11:05.873 --> 11:08.000
Department of Energy?
What do you think that means?

11:08.084 --> 11:10.044
It means government. Military.

11:10.127 --> 11:12.296
- [Dustin] Then why does it say "Energy"?
- Just trust me, all right?

11:12.380 --> 11:13.839
It's military. My dad's told me before.

11:13.923 --> 11:15.674
Mike's right. There's soldiers out front.

11:15.758 --> 11:17.802
Do they make, like,
lightbulbs or something?

11:17.885 --> 11:19.095
[Mike] No, weapons...

11:19.178 --> 11:20.679
to fight the Russians,
and commies and stuff.

11:20.763 --> 11:22.306
[Lucas] Weapons.

11:23.474 --> 11:25.768
[gasps] Oh, Jesus, this is bad.

11:25.851 --> 11:28.646
Really bad.
The place is like a fortress.

11:28.729 --> 11:29.772
Well, what do we do?

11:29.855 --> 11:31.524
[Mike] I don't know,
but we can't go home.

11:31.607 --> 11:33.025
We're fugitives now.

11:33.109 --> 11:35.403
[helicopter approaching]

11:35.486 --> 11:36.737
[stutters] Guys?

11:37.780 --> 11:39.573
Do you hear that?

11:45.621 --> 11:47.039
[Mike] Go, go, go, go!
[Dustin] Come on, come on!

11:47.123 --> 11:48.791
- It's stuck.
- Let's go, let's go, let's go!

11:48.874 --> 11:50.126
[Mike] Hurry up! Hurry, come on!
[Lucas] Come on!

11:50.209 --> 11:51.627
[Dustin] Go, go, go, go, go, go!

11:51.710 --> 11:53.170
[helicopter whirring]

11:53.254 --> 11:55.506
- [panting]
- [Lucas] Get down!

12:00.469 --> 12:01.804
[helicopter receding]

12:01.887 --> 12:03.264
Mental.

12:06.976 --> 12:08.185
[Joyce sighs]

12:10.354 --> 12:12.189
You say blood draws this thing?

12:12.273 --> 12:13.607
We don't know.

12:14.525 --> 12:15.860
It's just a theory.

12:19.947 --> 12:21.157
[Jonathan] I'm sorry, Mom.

12:21.240 --> 12:24.243
What, you're sorry?
You're... you're sorry?

12:24.326 --> 12:26.120
- That is not good enough, Jonathan.
- I know.

12:26.203 --> 12:28.622
That's not even close. That's not even
in the... in the ballpark.

12:28.706 --> 12:30.291
I wanted to tell you, I just--

12:30.374 --> 12:32.626
What if this thing took you, too?

12:32.710 --> 12:36.005
You risked your life... and Nancy's.

12:36.088 --> 12:39.550
[stammers] I thought I could save Will...
I still do.

12:39.633 --> 12:42.011
This is not yours to fix alone.

12:42.094 --> 12:46.932
[stammers] You act like you're all alone
out there in the world, but you're not.

12:47.016 --> 12:48.142
You're not alone.

12:48.225 --> 12:49.602
I know.

12:49.685 --> 12:51.103
[sighs] God damn it, Jonathan.

12:51.187 --> 12:53.898
- I know.
- Damn it.

12:54.648 --> 12:55.858
[sniffling]

12:56.817 --> 12:57.985
[Troy's mom] I want an apology!

12:58.068 --> 12:59.236
[Callahan] An apology for what, exactly?

12:59.320 --> 13:01.071
[Troy's mom] Where is the chief?
I want to speak to him

13:01.155 --> 13:02.490
- right this instant.
- Stay here.

13:02.573 --> 13:04.408
Ma'am, I need you to calm down.

13:04.492 --> 13:05.659
What is your name, Deputy?

13:05.743 --> 13:07.536
Well, I'm an officer...
[chuckles] okay?

13:07.620 --> 13:09.079
[Troy's mom] Name and badge number,
both of you!

13:09.163 --> 13:11.040
- What the hell is going on here?
- [Powell] Chief...

13:11.123 --> 13:13.083
These men are humiliating my son.

13:13.167 --> 13:15.169
- No, no, no. Okay, that's not true.
- Yes.

13:15.252 --> 13:16.629
There was some kind of fight, Chief--

13:16.712 --> 13:19.381
A psychotic child broke his arm!

13:19.465 --> 13:22.718
- A little girl, Chief. A little one.
- That tone! Do you hear that tone?

13:22.801 --> 13:24.053
Honestly,
I'm just trying to state a fact.

13:24.136 --> 13:25.554
- I don't have time for this.
- It was a little girl--

13:25.638 --> 13:28.224
Will you please take a statement...
[mouthing] and get her out?

13:28.307 --> 13:29.475
- [Callahan] Yes.
- So what'd this girl look like?

13:29.558 --> 13:32.728
She had no hair
and she was bleeding from her nose.

13:32.811 --> 13:34.730
Like a freak.

13:34.813 --> 13:35.940
What'd you just say?

13:36.649 --> 13:38.150
I said she's a freak!

13:38.234 --> 13:41.028
No, her hair.
What'd you say about her hair?

13:41.111 --> 13:43.030
Her head's shaved.

13:43.113 --> 13:44.865
She doesn't even look like a girl.

13:46.283 --> 13:47.284
And...

13:48.035 --> 13:49.119
And what?

13:50.454 --> 13:52.206
Tell the man, Troy.

13:54.375 --> 13:55.876
She can...

13:58.254 --> 13:59.421
do things.

13:59.505 --> 14:01.799
What kind of things?

14:01.882 --> 14:02.925
Like...

14:05.302 --> 14:06.345
make you fly.

14:09.306 --> 14:10.641
And piss yourself.

14:10.724 --> 14:11.725
What?

14:13.310 --> 14:14.311
Was she alone?

14:15.771 --> 14:17.606
She always hangs out with those losers.

14:17.690 --> 14:18.857
"Losers"?

14:19.900 --> 14:21.485
What losers?

14:25.447 --> 14:26.657
Hey.

14:27.783 --> 14:29.285
You owe me $1.20.

14:31.078 --> 14:33.414
Don't worry, he'll need more than aspirin
when we're done with him.

14:33.497 --> 14:36.166
Yeah, if the creep ever gets out.

14:36.250 --> 14:37.835
The cops should just lock him up forever.

14:37.918 --> 14:40.504
- Did you see the look on his face?
- [Steve groans]

14:40.588 --> 14:42.423
- Oh.
- [chuckles]

14:42.506 --> 14:44.842
He probably had that same look
whenever he killed his brother, right?

14:44.925 --> 14:49.430
Oh, God, I just got an image
of him making that face

14:49.513 --> 14:50.848
- while he and Nancy are screwing.
- [chuckles]

14:50.931 --> 14:52.766
Carol, for once in your life,
shut your damn mouth!

14:52.850 --> 14:55.561
- What?
- Hey, what's your problem, man?

14:57.313 --> 14:58.981
You're both assholes.
That's my problem.

14:59.064 --> 15:00.399
- Are you serious right now, man?
- Yeah, I'm serious.

15:00.482 --> 15:01.483
You shouldn't have done that.

15:01.567 --> 15:02.860
- Done what?
- You know what.

15:02.943 --> 15:04.820
You mean call her out
for what she really is?

15:04.904 --> 15:07.156
Oh, that's funny, because I don't remember
you asking me to stop.

15:07.239 --> 15:08.908
I should've put that spray paint
right down your throat.

15:08.991 --> 15:10.618
- What the hell, Steve?
- [Steve] You know,

15:10.701 --> 15:12.786
neither of you ever cared about her.
You never even liked her,

15:12.870 --> 15:14.538
because she's not miserable like you two.

15:14.622 --> 15:16.040
She actually cares about other people.

15:16.123 --> 15:17.374
The slut with a heart of gold.

15:17.458 --> 15:18.667
I told you to watch your mouth!

15:18.751 --> 15:21.045
Hey! I don't know
what's gotten into you, man,

15:21.128 --> 15:23.422
- but you don't talk to her that way.
- Get out of my face.

15:23.505 --> 15:25.007
- Or what?
- [grunts]

15:25.090 --> 15:26.175
Or what?

15:26.258 --> 15:27.843
You gonna fight me now, too? Huh?

15:27.927 --> 15:29.011
You gonna fight me now, too?

15:29.094 --> 15:31.388
Because you couldn't take
Jonathan Byers...

15:32.389 --> 15:35.225
so I wouldn't recommend that.

15:40.981 --> 15:42.316
[car door opens]

15:42.399 --> 15:44.401
- Here, let me get the door for you, buddy.
- [door slams]

15:44.485 --> 15:47.279
That's right.
Run away, Stevie boy!

15:47.363 --> 15:49.865
Run away!
Just like you always do.

15:49.949 --> 15:53.285
That Nancy's turning you
into a little pussy!

15:54.203 --> 15:56.664
- [tires screeching]
- That's right, Harrington, run away!

15:56.747 --> 15:59.375
Run away! [scoffs]

16:09.134 --> 16:10.552
[Nancy] I have to go home.

16:10.636 --> 16:12.137
No, you can't.

16:13.138 --> 16:15.975
- My mom... my dad are there.
- They're gonna be okay.

16:17.643 --> 16:19.520
- Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey.
- Let go.

16:19.603 --> 16:21.230
- Let go!
- Hey! Listen to me. Listen to me.

16:21.313 --> 16:22.773
The last thing in the world we need

16:22.856 --> 16:24.566
is them knowing
you're mixed up in all this.

16:24.650 --> 16:27.194
- Mike is over there--
- They haven't found him.

16:27.277 --> 16:28.570
Not yet, at least.

16:28.654 --> 16:30.322
[helicopter whirring]

16:31.240 --> 16:32.908
- For Mike?
- Come on, get in the car.

16:36.078 --> 16:38.372
Look, we need to find them
before they do.

16:38.455 --> 16:39.790
Do you have any idea
where he might have gone?

16:39.873 --> 16:42.668
- No, I don't.
- I need you to think.

16:42.751 --> 16:44.461
I don't know.
We haven't talked a lot.

16:44.545 --> 16:46.380
I mean, lately... [sighs]

16:46.463 --> 16:47.631
Is there any place that your...

16:47.715 --> 16:49.675
your parents don't know
about that he might go?

16:49.758 --> 16:51.885
- [stuttering] I don't know.
- I might.

16:51.969 --> 16:53.053
What?

16:53.137 --> 16:57.141
I don't know where he is,
but I think I know how to ask him.

17:06.442 --> 17:07.609
Whoa.

17:15.409 --> 17:16.702
I got it.

17:22.833 --> 17:24.626
[helicopter hovering]

17:24.710 --> 17:28.255
[Nancy on radio] Mike,
are you there? Mike?

17:28.338 --> 17:29.673
You guys hear that?

17:29.757 --> 17:31.884
Mike, it's me, Nancy.

17:34.178 --> 17:35.637
Mike, are you there?

17:35.721 --> 17:37.389
Answer.

17:37.473 --> 17:39.141
Mike, we need you to answer.

17:39.224 --> 17:40.768
Is that your sister?

17:41.727 --> 17:44.396
This is an emergency, Mike.

17:44.480 --> 17:45.773
Do you copy?

17:47.024 --> 17:48.442
Mike, do you copy?

17:48.525 --> 17:50.069
Okay, this is really weird.

17:50.152 --> 17:51.653
Don't answer.

17:51.737 --> 17:53.822
- She said it was an emergency.
- What if it's a trick?

17:53.906 --> 17:56.658
- It's your sister!
- What if the bad people kidnapped her?

17:56.742 --> 17:59.620
- What if they're forcing her to say this?
- I need you to answer.

17:59.703 --> 18:02.247
It's like Lando Calrissian.
Don't answer.

18:02.331 --> 18:04.083
We need to know
that you're there, Mike.

18:04.792 --> 18:07.628
Listen, kid, this is the chief.
If you're there, pick up.

18:07.711 --> 18:09.713
We know you're in trouble
and we know about the girl.

18:09.797 --> 18:11.840
Why is she with the chief?

18:11.924 --> 18:13.217
How the hell does he know about...

18:13.300 --> 18:17.221
[Hopper] We can protect you,
we can help you, but you gotta pick up.

18:17.304 --> 18:19.932
Are you there?
Do you copy? Over.

18:22.851 --> 18:23.936
[sighs]

18:27.064 --> 18:28.857
Anybody got any other ideas?

18:30.442 --> 18:31.944
[Mike] Yeah, I copy.

18:33.946 --> 18:34.988
It's Mike.

18:35.072 --> 18:36.406
I'm here.

18:38.784 --> 18:40.035
We're here.

18:49.670 --> 18:51.171
[Steve] Need a hand?

18:52.798 --> 18:54.424
Did you have something
to do with this?

18:55.425 --> 18:56.593
I just...

18:57.594 --> 18:58.762
I wanna help.

19:07.104 --> 19:08.480
All yours.

19:21.326 --> 19:25.080
[sighs] They expect us
to just sit here like prisoners.

19:25.164 --> 19:26.790
We should be out there looking for him.

19:26.874 --> 19:29.668
Honey, we have to trust them, okay?

19:29.751 --> 19:32.546
This is our government.
They're on our side.

19:32.629 --> 19:33.630
[Karen sighs]

19:35.048 --> 19:36.550
That man gives me the creeps.

19:39.094 --> 19:40.262
Nancy.

19:40.345 --> 19:42.806
You don't think
she's involved in this, too, do you?

19:42.890 --> 19:44.308
Nancy with Mike?

19:44.391 --> 19:45.851
[chuckles] No.

19:46.768 --> 19:48.937
- No.
- [sighs]

19:52.316 --> 19:54.151
[Dustin breathing heavily]

20:00.449 --> 20:01.783
Will you stop pacing?

20:01.867 --> 20:03.827
It's been way too long.

20:03.911 --> 20:06.830
Do you know what? Maybe you're right.
Maybe this is all a trap

20:06.914 --> 20:08.624
and the bad men
are coming to get us right now!

20:08.707 --> 20:09.708
It's not a trap.

20:09.791 --> 20:11.793
Why would the chief set us up?

20:11.877 --> 20:14.046
Nancy, maybe, but the chief?

20:14.129 --> 20:15.505
Lando Calrissian.

20:15.589 --> 20:17.257
Would you shut up about Lando?

20:17.341 --> 20:19.259
I don't feel good about this.
I don't feel good about this!

20:19.343 --> 20:21.178
[shouting] When do you feel good
about anything?

20:22.512 --> 20:24.306
[vehicles approaching]

20:33.190 --> 20:34.233
[Dustin] Shit!

20:34.316 --> 20:35.651
[Mike] Go, go, go, go.

20:37.903 --> 20:39.613
[panting] Lando.

20:39.696 --> 20:41.448
You think they saw us?

20:41.531 --> 20:43.200
Both of you, shut up.

21:26.743 --> 21:28.245
[grunts]

21:28.328 --> 21:29.454
- [man 1] Hey!
- [blows landing]

21:29.538 --> 21:30.831
[man 1 grunts]

21:30.914 --> 21:32.249
[man 2] What the--
[grunting]

21:33.542 --> 21:35.544
[door creaks]

21:37.921 --> 21:39.923
[breathing heavily] All right, let's go.

21:41.633 --> 21:43.260
Let's go!

22:06.450 --> 22:08.785
Mike. Oh, my God. Mike!

22:12.622 --> 22:14.666
I was so worried about you.

22:14.750 --> 22:17.169
Yeah, uh... me, too.

22:22.549 --> 22:23.884
Is that my dress?

22:27.262 --> 22:30.557
Okay, so, in this example,
we're the acrobat.

22:30.640 --> 22:33.560
Will and Barbara, and that monster,
they're this flea.

22:33.643 --> 22:36.021
And this is the Upside Down,
where Will is hiding.

22:36.104 --> 22:39.566
Mr. Clarke said the only way to get there
is through a rip of time and space.

22:39.649 --> 22:41.234
- A gate.
- That we tracked to Hawkins Lab.

22:41.318 --> 22:42.611
With our compasses.

22:44.571 --> 22:47.824
Okay, so the gate
has a really strong electromagnetic field,

22:47.908 --> 22:50.118
and that can change
the directions of a compass needle.

22:50.202 --> 22:51.411
Is this gate underground?

22:51.495 --> 22:53.163
[Eleven] Yes.

22:54.498 --> 22:56.249
Near a large water tank?

22:56.958 --> 22:58.126
Yes.

22:59.002 --> 23:00.462
[stutters] How do you know all that?

23:01.838 --> 23:03.632
He's seen it.

23:03.715 --> 23:05.550
[Joyce] Is there any way that you could...

23:06.843 --> 23:09.304
that you could reach Will?
That you could talk to him in this--

23:09.387 --> 23:10.472
The Upside Down.

23:10.555 --> 23:12.182
[whispering] Down. Yeah.

23:13.850 --> 23:14.976
[Nancy] And my friend Barbara?

23:15.060 --> 23:16.520
Can you find her, too?

23:20.565 --> 23:22.442
[static]

23:29.116 --> 23:30.784
[static increases]

23:45.215 --> 23:46.716
[static becomes faint]

23:52.806 --> 23:53.849
I'm sorry.

23:53.932 --> 23:54.975
What?

23:55.058 --> 23:57.185
[stuttering] What's wrong?
What happened?

23:57.310 --> 23:59.938
[voice breaks] I can't find them.

24:24.462 --> 24:25.797
[turns faucet off]

24:33.430 --> 24:35.724
[Mike] Whenever she uses her powers,
she gets weak.

24:35.807 --> 24:38.351
The more energy she uses,
the more tired she gets.

24:38.435 --> 24:41.021
- Like, she flipped the van earlier.
- It was awesome.

24:41.104 --> 24:43.398
- But she's drained.
- Like a bad battery.

24:43.481 --> 24:46.359
Well... [stutters]
How do we make her better?

24:46.443 --> 24:49.279
We don't.
We just have to wait and try again.

24:49.362 --> 24:51.198
[Nancy] Well, how long?

24:51.281 --> 24:52.657
I don't know.

24:52.741 --> 24:53.992
[Eleven] The bath.

24:54.075 --> 24:55.327
[Joyce] What?

24:57.954 --> 24:59.623
I can find them.

25:01.124 --> 25:02.167
In the bath.

25:05.128 --> 25:06.463
[screaming]

25:07.380 --> 25:08.548
[woman] Oh!

25:10.717 --> 25:12.969
Oh. Oh, my...
No, mmm-mmm.

25:13.053 --> 25:15.055
Hey, you know how they did that?
You know what that is?

25:15.138 --> 25:16.389
[sighing] No, what?

25:16.473 --> 25:19.017
Melted plastic
and microwaved bubble gum.

25:19.100 --> 25:20.977
[woman] No way. Really?

25:21.061 --> 25:22.604
Really.

25:22.729 --> 25:24.272
[phone ringing]

25:25.106 --> 25:27.067
- What in the world?
- Do you want me to pause it?

25:27.150 --> 25:28.735
I'm sure it's just a wrong number.

25:31.696 --> 25:32.739
Hello?

25:32.822 --> 25:34.616
Mr. Clarke? It's Dustin.

25:34.699 --> 25:37.577
Dustin? Is everything okay?

25:37.661 --> 25:39.287
Yeah, yeah. I just, I...

25:39.371 --> 25:41.456
I have a science question.

25:41.539 --> 25:44.918
It's ten o'clock on Saturday.
Why don't we pick this up--

25:45.001 --> 25:47.963
Do you know anything
about sensory deprivation tanks?

25:48.046 --> 25:49.839
Specifically how to build one?

25:49.923 --> 25:52.884
Sensory deprivation?
[stutters] What is this for?

25:53.593 --> 25:55.178
Fun.

25:55.262 --> 25:56.930
Okay. Well...

25:57.847 --> 26:00.183
Why don't we talk about it Monday?
After school, okay?

26:00.267 --> 26:02.727
You always say
we should never stop being curious.

26:02.811 --> 26:04.729
To always open any curiosity door we find.

26:04.813 --> 26:05.855
Dustin--

26:05.939 --> 26:08.566
Why are you keeping
this curiosity door locked?

26:09.901 --> 26:11.111
[sighs]

26:11.194 --> 26:12.404
Uh-huh.

26:12.487 --> 26:14.197
[indistinct chatter over phone]

26:16.032 --> 26:17.450
Uh-huh. How much?

26:18.368 --> 26:19.411
Uh-huh.

26:20.704 --> 26:23.498
Yep, all right.
Yeah, we'll be careful.

26:23.581 --> 26:25.208
Definitely.
All right, Mr. Clarke.

26:25.292 --> 26:27.502
Yeah, I'll see you on Monday.
I'll see you on Monday, Mr. Clarke.

26:27.585 --> 26:28.962
Bye.

26:29.045 --> 26:31.339
Do you still have that kiddie pool
we bobbed for apples in?

26:31.423 --> 26:33.717
- I think so. Yeah.
- Yeah.

26:33.800 --> 26:35.468
Good. Then we just need salt.
Lots of it.

26:35.552 --> 26:37.262
How much is "lots"?

26:39.347 --> 26:40.432
1,500 pounds.

26:41.141 --> 26:43.226
Well, where are we gonna
get that much salt?

26:52.694 --> 26:54.404
[Jonathan grunting]

26:57.949 --> 26:59.326
Hey, wait.

26:59.409 --> 27:01.369
It's not gonna snow next week, is it?

27:01.453 --> 27:03.538
[sighs] Worst case, no school.

27:03.621 --> 27:06.333
Even if we find Will in there...

27:06.416 --> 27:07.959
what are we gonna do about that thing?

27:08.043 --> 27:09.336
We're not gonna do anything.

27:09.419 --> 27:10.837
I don't want you
anywhere near this, all right?

27:10.920 --> 27:13.340
- Your mom's been through enough already.
- He's my brother.

27:13.423 --> 27:16.760
Listen to me.
I'm gonna find him. All right?

27:16.843 --> 27:18.386
You gotta trust me on this.

27:18.470 --> 27:20.180
I am going to find him.

27:26.728 --> 27:28.688
[grunting] This damn thing is heavy.

27:34.903 --> 27:36.654
Come on.
It's upside down.

27:36.738 --> 27:37.989
[Lucas] No, this way.

27:40.867 --> 27:42.035
- Okay, um...
- How does this even work?

27:42.118 --> 27:44.621
- Try that side.
- [grunts] Son of a bitch!

27:44.704 --> 27:46.706
- Pull it back. Pull it back.
- I am!

27:46.790 --> 27:49.417
- [Lucas] One, two, three.
- [grunts]

27:49.501 --> 27:50.835
Shit!

27:59.177 --> 28:00.470
[grunts] Ah.

28:00.553 --> 28:01.638
[Nancy] Stand back.

28:08.478 --> 28:10.105
Whoa.

28:19.906 --> 28:21.825
[Nancy] What did she even eat?

28:21.908 --> 28:24.536
- [Mike] What?
- Eleven.

28:24.619 --> 28:28.873
[Mike] Oh.
Candy, leftovers, Eggos...

28:30.375 --> 28:32.210
She really likes Eggos.

28:33.420 --> 28:35.505
[Nancy] I knew you
were acting weird. I just...

28:35.588 --> 28:37.632
I thought it was because of Will.

28:37.715 --> 28:40.593
I knew you were acting weird, too.
I thought it was 'cause of Steve.

28:42.011 --> 28:43.096
Hey...

28:45.223 --> 28:47.016
No more secrets, okay?

28:47.100 --> 28:49.144
From now on we tell each other everything.

28:49.227 --> 28:52.272
Okay. Do you like Jonathan now?

28:52.355 --> 28:54.315
What? No.

28:55.275 --> 28:58.069
No, it's... it's not...
it's not like that.

28:59.654 --> 29:00.905
Do you like Eleven?

29:00.989 --> 29:04.325
What? No. Ew. Gross.

29:17.213 --> 29:20.508
This will keep it dark for you.

29:20.592 --> 29:22.677
Just like in your bathtub.

29:24.179 --> 29:25.722
[sighs]

29:25.805 --> 29:27.515
You're a very brave girl.

29:27.599 --> 29:29.392
You know that, don't you?

29:30.435 --> 29:34.397
Everything you're doing
for my boy... for Will...

29:35.899 --> 29:37.484
for my family...

29:38.485 --> 29:39.527
[sighs]

29:39.611 --> 29:41.738
[sniffs] Thank you.

29:45.325 --> 29:46.576
Listen.

29:47.160 --> 29:50.955
I am gonna be there
with you the whole time.

29:51.039 --> 29:52.999
And if it ever gets too scary...

29:53.082 --> 29:57.462
[stutters] in that place,
you just let me know, okay?

30:00.507 --> 30:01.549
Yes.

30:04.219 --> 30:05.261
Ready?

30:06.846 --> 30:08.306
[breath trembling]

30:10.183 --> 30:11.226
Ready.

30:28.618 --> 30:30.203
Colder!

30:32.163 --> 30:33.456
Warmer!

30:35.792 --> 30:37.252
Right there!

31:10.827 --> 31:12.453
[static]

31:31.264 --> 31:32.473
[sighs]

31:50.658 --> 31:52.368
[electricity surging]

32:11.304 --> 32:13.014
[breathing heavily]

32:55.098 --> 32:56.140
Barb?

32:56.224 --> 32:57.475
Barbara?

33:00.311 --> 33:02.063
[breathing heavily]

33:17.495 --> 33:18.955
[squelching]

33:22.208 --> 33:23.918
[bubbling]

33:24.002 --> 33:24.919
[gasps]

33:25.003 --> 33:26.462
[breathing heavily]

33:26.546 --> 33:27.922
[electricity pulsating]

33:28.840 --> 33:30.883
- What's going on?
- I don't know.

33:31.843 --> 33:34.887
Is Barb okay?
Is she okay?

33:34.971 --> 33:36.973
[screaming] Gone! Gone!

33:37.056 --> 33:38.808
Gone!

33:38.891 --> 33:41.561
Gone! Gone!

33:41.644 --> 33:43.938
Gone. Gone.

33:44.022 --> 33:45.523
- [crying]
- [Eleven] Gone.

33:45.606 --> 33:47.400
[Joyce] It's okay.
It's okay. It's okay.

33:47.483 --> 33:49.777
- [Eleven] Gone. Gone!
- It's okay. It's okay.

33:49.861 --> 33:51.279
Gone!

33:51.362 --> 33:53.114
- [Joyce] Hey. It's okay.
- [gasping]

33:53.197 --> 33:55.700
It's okay, we're right here.
We're right here, honey.

33:55.783 --> 33:59.037
[Joyce echoing]
It's okay. I got you.

33:59.120 --> 34:01.956
Don't be afraid.

34:02.040 --> 34:03.541
I'm right here with you.

34:03.624 --> 34:06.169
I'm right here with you.

34:06.252 --> 34:08.421
It's okay. It's okay.

34:08.504 --> 34:10.798
[echoing] It's okay.

34:10.882 --> 34:13.009
It's okay, you're safe.

34:13.092 --> 34:14.469
You're okay, honey.

34:15.344 --> 34:16.971
[Eleven] Castle Byers.

34:17.555 --> 34:18.931
Castle Byers.

34:58.346 --> 34:59.388
Will.

34:59.472 --> 35:01.307
- Will?
- [gasps]

35:06.729 --> 35:08.731
You tell him...
tell him I'm coming.

35:08.815 --> 35:10.316
[echoing] Mom is coming.

35:10.399 --> 35:12.527
Your mom...
[stutters] she's coming for you.

35:15.530 --> 35:16.531
[muttering weakly] Hurry.

35:17.115 --> 35:18.157
[on radio] Hurry.

35:20.493 --> 35:23.621
Okay. Listen, you tell him to...
[stutters] to stay where he is.

35:23.704 --> 35:26.707
We're coming. We're coming, okay?
We're coming, honey.

35:26.791 --> 35:29.043
Just... just hold on a little longer.

35:29.127 --> 35:31.212
Will. Will.

35:36.342 --> 35:37.969
[low growling]

35:42.431 --> 35:43.558
Will?

35:44.475 --> 35:45.560
Will!

35:46.769 --> 35:49.397
[panting, whimpering]

35:50.064 --> 35:51.774
[whimpering on radio]

35:52.567 --> 35:54.277
- [both gasp]
- Oh!

35:54.360 --> 35:57.071
- [Eleven breathing heavily]
- Oh, okay, okay.

35:58.281 --> 35:59.323
I've got you.

36:00.783 --> 36:02.618
It's okay.
I got you. I got you.

36:03.244 --> 36:05.872
I got you, honey.
You did so good.

36:08.249 --> 36:10.334
- Are you okay?
- [Eleven cries]

36:11.627 --> 36:13.880
[Hopper sighs] So this fort.
Where is it?

36:13.963 --> 36:15.756
[stutters] Uh, it's in the woods
behind our house.

36:15.840 --> 36:18.259
Yeah, he used to go there to hide.

36:24.015 --> 36:25.266
Hey, get back inside.

36:25.349 --> 36:26.475
What, are you insane?

36:26.559 --> 36:27.852
- No, I'm--
- Look, if something happens to me,

36:27.935 --> 36:28.978
I don't make it back--

36:29.061 --> 36:30.771
Yeah, but then I'll go.
You stay.

36:30.855 --> 36:31.981
Are you kidding me?

36:32.064 --> 36:35.318
He's my son, Hop. My son.

36:35.401 --> 36:36.485
I'm going!

36:37.612 --> 36:39.322
- Now, listen, I need you to stay here...
- [Jonathan] No.

36:39.405 --> 36:40.740
- ...and watch over the kids.
- No, Mom.

36:40.823 --> 36:42.658
- I can help.
- Please, I need you to stay, Jonathan.

36:42.742 --> 36:43.743
Joyce!

36:43.826 --> 36:44.994
- Please.
- Please, be careful.

36:45.077 --> 36:46.621
- [Hopper] Joyce, come on!
- Please. I'm gonna find him.

36:46.704 --> 36:48.456
I'm gonna find him.

36:48.539 --> 36:49.916
[engine starting]

36:50.833 --> 36:51.918
[door closes]

36:52.501 --> 36:54.003
[tires screeching]

36:59.884 --> 37:01.219
[door opens]

37:03.304 --> 37:04.513
[door slams]

37:22.782 --> 37:24.825
We have to go back to the station.

37:26.285 --> 37:27.328
What?

37:28.246 --> 37:33.834
Your mom and Hopper
are just walking in there like bait.

37:34.919 --> 37:37.838
That thing is still in there.

37:39.882 --> 37:43.261
And we can't just sit here
and let it get them, too.

37:43.344 --> 37:44.637
We can't.

37:48.766 --> 37:50.977
[sighs] You still wanna try it out?

37:51.727 --> 37:54.063
I wanna finish what we started.

37:55.773 --> 37:57.650
I want to kill it.

38:12.164 --> 38:13.708
So this is your plan?

38:13.791 --> 38:15.501
Worked for me before, didn't it?

38:15.584 --> 38:17.795
- Well, did it?
- Come on, trust me.

38:19.046 --> 38:21.007
[announcer on radio] I'd like to hear
your thoughts on the war.

38:21.090 --> 38:23.092
I think we're dealing with a whole
different environment here.

38:23.175 --> 38:24.844
[announcer 2] I'll tell you what,
we always planned

38:24.927 --> 38:27.221
on the Russians massing the fire and we...

38:42.862 --> 38:44.030
[Hopper sighs]

38:44.864 --> 38:45.948
- [Joyce gasps]
- [man] Don't move!

38:46.991 --> 38:48.701
- All right, move in.
- [guns cocking]

38:48.784 --> 38:50.244
It's all right.

38:50.328 --> 38:51.704
Let me do the talking.

38:51.787 --> 38:53.289
[indistinct radio chatter]

38:58.419 --> 39:00.588
[Will softly]
♪ If I go there will be trouble ♪

39:00.671 --> 39:01.756
[shuddering]

39:01.839 --> 39:04.633
♪ And if I stay it will be double ♪

39:05.718 --> 39:08.429
♪ So, come on and let me know ♪

39:09.472 --> 39:11.557
♪ Should I stay or should I go now? ♪

39:11.640 --> 39:13.351
[monster growling]

39:14.560 --> 39:16.187
[footsteps approaching]

39:22.485 --> 39:24.236
[growling continues]

39:28.199 --> 39:29.450
[breathing heavily]

39:29.533 --> 39:31.243
[growling]

39:31.327 --> 39:32.745
[growling stops]

39:36.707 --> 39:37.708
[monster growls]
